  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **ween1992ontheroad-t01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween1992ontheroad-t02**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween1992ontheroad-t03**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween1992ontheroad-t04**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween1992ontheroad-t05**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween1992ontheroad-t06**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween1992ontheroad-t07**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween1992ontheroad-t08**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween1992ontheroad** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 25 songs; 85 min [1]. Said about its sound: Start of track 1, end of track 24 and all of track 25 were patched with a worse-sounding but more complete copy [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Two tracks that were officially released have been removed from this compilation of 1992 on-the-road recordings [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween1992ontheroad**: taped by Kirk Miller; source: SBD/AUD Cassette Masters > 2nd Gen [1]. Also: Master soundboard/audience cassettes, second generation; compiled, recorded and mixed by Kirk Miller, then merged and remastered by Johnny in April 2021 [1]",
